# Secret of Bloodbending with its additional cost "waterbend {10}" paid (CR 701.67a-b): "you control that player during their next turn
# instead" of their next combat phase, as Mindslaver would (CR 723.1). {U}{U}{U}{U} come from Black Lotus and Mox Sapphire; the ten generic
# are Mana Vault's three and Sol Ring's two, which are in the pool, and five Memnites tapped, which are no {T} cost (so the ones that came this
# turn count). While it waits the control is "Bot1" with no "+combat". It governs all of Bot2's turn 8, its first main phase and its combat and
# its second main phase, and is over on turn 9. The spell has exiled itself, as the unpaid version does.

